81 @@\\n 36|            - hit: int (0/1) if enabled by runner\\n 37|      - batch_size: int\\n 38|      - seed: int\\n 39| -\\n 40| +    \\n 41|      Output:\\n 42|      - list[int] of NEW candidate indices (no repeats; already-selected may be ignored/replaced by runner).\\n 43| -\\n 44| -    You may implement any suitable algorithmic model here, including but not limited to:\\n 45| -    traditional algorithms, machine learning models, deep learning models, biological models,\\n 46| -    and mathematical models.\\n 47| +    \\n 48| +    Strategy: Hybrid exploration-exploitation with adaptive sampling\\n 49| +    - Early rounds: More random exploration\\n 50| +    - Later rounds: More exploitation of high-scoring candidates\\n 51| +    - Always maintain some diversity\\n 52|      \\"\\"\\"\\n 53| -    pass\\n 54| +    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n 55| +    \\n 56| +    # Get already selected indices\\n 57| +    selected = set(h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in history)\\n 58| +    \\n 59| +    # Get all available candidate indices\\n 60| +    all_indices = list(range(len(candidates)))\\n 61| +    available = [i for i in all_indices if i not in selected]\\n 62| +    \\n 63| +    if len(available) <= batch_size:\\n 64| +        return available\\n 65| +    \\n 66| +    # Calculate exploration ratio based on history size\\n 67| +    # More exploration in early rounds, more exploitation later\\n 68| +    num_rounds = len(history) // batch_size if batch_size > 0 else 0\\n 69| +    exploration_ratio = max(0.3, 0.8 - 0.15 * num_rounds)  # Starts at 80%, decreases to 30%\\n 70| +    \\n 71| +    # Separate exploration and exploitation\\n 72| +    num_explore = int(batch_size * exploration_ratio)\\n 73| +    num_exploit = batch_size - num_explore\\n 74| +    \\n 75| +    # Exploration: random sampling\\n 76| +    explore_indices = rng.sample(available, min(num_explore, len(available)))\\n 77| +    \\n 78| +    # Exploitation: select based on scores\\n 79| +    if len(history) > 0